  30:     - Right of divider: a single gray (5) start pixel.
  31: 
  32:     Rule:
  33:     - Remove the divider; shift the gray start into the left canvas.
  34:     - Read glyphs in column-major order (left→right, top→bottom).
  35:     - Each glyph's shape (pixel area) encodes a segment: area 4 → down 2, area 5 → right 3, area 6 → left 4, area 7 → left 2.
  36:     - Append segments sequentially, stepping down one cell between each.
  37: 
  38:     Key insight: Glyph pixel count (area) uniquely determines both segment length and direction — the shape itself is the instruction.
  39:     """
