/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:30:    "main_doc_head": "Fill the framed placeholders with matched sprites, then recolor them through split edge legends.\n\nInput structure:\n- A single gray rectangular frame encloses solid source-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n- Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template per placeholder color.\n- Legend entries are split across the grid boundary: top or left fragments show transformed shape clues in\n  one shared ink color, while the paired bottom or right fragments show only the target recolor.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:40:    "main_doc_head": "Copy two-color sprites into the frame by matching their dominant color and recoloring only that color class.\n\nInput structure:\n- A background grid contains one rectangular gray frame whose interior holds solid NxN placeholder blocks.\n- Outside the frame there is one two-color sprite per placeholder color, plus compact two-color legend glyphs that\n  encode placeholder-color -> target-color mappings.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:70:    "main_doc_head": "Rebuild the framed output by combining color-matched sprites, quadrant-based rotation, and rotating multicolor legend tiles.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses solid-color square placeholder blocks arranged on a regular grid.\n- Outside the frame sit one monochrome sprite template per placeholder color and one opaque rectangular legend per color; each legend has a source-color tag column and an NxN multicolor pattern sample.\n\nRule:\n- Detect the frame, all placeholder blocks inside it, the matching-color sprite masks outside it, and the pattern tile stored in each legend."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:90:    "main_doc_head": "Replace framed placeholders with counted sprites and recolor them via a filtered count legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses solid-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n- Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template for each placeholder color.\n- The top-left band contains compact monochrome legend entries whose colored pixel counts encode lookup keys,\n  and some of those legend counts are distractors unused by any real sprite.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:100:    "main_doc_head": "Rebuild the framed arrangement on the full canvas and draw color-coded motion trails.\n\nInput structure:\n- Background plus one grey rectangular frame whose interior contains solid placeholder blocks.\n- Outside the frame: one sprite template per placeholder color and one 3x4 legend per color.\n- In this fused variant the source sprites sit in exterior lanes that can visually connect to the frame.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:110:    "main_doc_head": "Place one recolored sprite at a time, letting earlier placements block later searches.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses repeated solid placeholder blocks of several colors on a\n  regular lattice.\n- Outside the frame there is one sprite template per placeholder color plus one two-color legend\n  per placeholder color; in generated samples the sprites form a readable row above the frame.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:130:    "main_doc_head": "Fill a partitioned frame with recolored sprites whose orientation is decided per chamber.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses solid placeholder blocks, and a gray divider splits the frame interior into left/right chambers.\n- Outside the frame there is one sprite template per placeholder color plus two legend groups, one fully left of the frame and one fully right of it.\n\nRule:\n- Detect the frame, recover the two chambers from the internal divider, and assign every placeholder block to exactly one chamber."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:150:    "main_doc_head": "Stamp external sprites into the frame, then recolor them by a mirrored bottom-right spatial legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- The canvas background contains one gray rectangular frame with solid colored placeholders inside.\n- The bottom-right corner of the whole canvas contains a fixed 5x5 legend panel with four colored 2x2 blocks.\n- Outside the frame and outside that corner panel: one sprite template per placeholder color.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:160:    "main_doc_head": "Recolor and place outlined hollow sprites into the framed workspace.\n\nInput structure:\n- The canvas has one rectangular gray frame whose interior contains solid-color placeholder blocks.\n- Outside the frame, each placeholder color has a same-color sprite template; these templates are hollow shapes with enclosed background holes.\n- The outside area also contains compact two-color legend glyphs that map placeholder colors to their final output colors.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:170:    "main_doc_head": "Copy same-colored sprite templates into a framed placeholder layout while leaving all outside objects visible.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background, one rectangular gray frame, and solid colored placeholder blocks inside the frame.\n- Outside the frame: one real sprite template per placeholder color plus a compact two-color legend block for each color.\n\nRule:\n- Find the frame and the placeholder blocks inside it."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:190:    "main_doc_head": "Split the solved multi-frame scene into target-color panels that aggregate across frames.\n\nInput structure:\n- A background canvas contains 2-3 disjoint grey rectangular frames, each with solid placeholder blocks inside.\n- Outside the whole framed region are same-color sprite templates and compact two-color legend glyphs.\n\nRule:\n- Find every frame, recover which placeholder colors belong to each frame, and match each source color to its external sprite and legend target."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:200:    "main_doc_head": "Recolor outside sprites through a color table before placing them into the framed region.\n\nInput structure:\n- A background canvas contains one gray rectangular frame whose interior holds solid NxN target-color placeholders.\n- Outside the frame are source-colored sprite templates and, in the upper-left corner, a compact Kx4 color\n  lookup table with rows of the form [src, src, tgt, tgt].\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:210:    "main_doc_head": "Copy recolored sprites into a framed region while keeping the surrounding panorama intact.\n\nInput structure:\n- A bg canvas contains one grey rectangular frame whose interior holds solid colored placeholder blocks.\n- Outside the frame, one sprite template per placeholder color is scattered around the top, bottom, left, and right\n  of the frame rather than being packed on one side.\n- Small two-color legend glyphs elsewhere outside the frame map each placeholder color to its output color.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:230:    "main_doc_head": "Rebuild the framed output by combining split edge legends, shape matching up to transform, and quadrant-based placement rotation.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses solid placeholder blocks of one shared square size.\n- Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template per placeholder color.\n- Along the outer boundary, legend entries are scattered across different edges: the top or left fragment shows a silhouette in one common legend-ink color, while the opposite bottom or right fragment supplies the target color for the same span.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:240:    "main_doc_head": "Copy two-color sprites into the frame, but recolor only their dominant-color pixels when a legend entry exists.\n\nInput structure:\n- One rectangular gray frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks laid out on the background.\n- Outside the frame there is one connected two-color sprite for every placeholder color; the larger-area color is\n  the sprite's primary color and matches the placeholder.\n- Also outside the frame are compact two-color legend glyphs for only some placeholder colors, so the legend set is\n  intentionally incomplete."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:250:    "main_doc_head": "Stamp frame-selected patterned sprites into a framed region using outside sprite templates and paired multicolor legends.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background, one rectangular non-gray frame, and solid square placeholder blocks inside that frame.\n- Outside the frame: one monochrome sprite template per placeholder color, plus two opaque N x (N+1) legends for each source color.\n  Each legend starts with a uniform source-color column and its right N x N tile is either a striped or checkerboard pattern sample.\n\nRule:"
